# DAX Measures Documentation

This document outlines the key DAX measures used to build the Sales Dashboard. The measures are grouped by their functionality.

These measures utilize the What-If `Parameter[Select Year Value]` to dynamically calculate Current Year (CY) and Previous Year (PY) metrics.

## Parameter = GENERATESERIES(2020, 2023, 1)

## DAX:
-- Base Measures:
Total Sales = SUM(Orders[Sales])
Total Profit = SUM(Orders[Profit])
Total Quantity = SUM(Orders[Quantity])

----------

Current Year = 'Parameter'[Select Year Value]
Previous Year = 'Parameter'[Select Year Value] - 1

- CY Sales = 
VAR Selected_Year = Parameter[Select Year Value]
RETURN CALCULATE([Total Sales], YEAR(Orders[Order Date]) = Selected_Year)

- PY Sales = 
VAR SelectYear = Parameter[Select Year Value]
RETURN CALCULATE([Total Sales], YEAR(Orders[Order Date]) = SelectYear - 1)

- CY Profit = 
VAR SelectYear = Parameter[Select Year Value]
RETURN CALCULATE([Total Profit], YEAR(Orders[Order Date]) = SelectYear)

- PY Profit = 
VAR SelectYear = Parameter[Select Year Value]
RETURN CALCULATE([Total Profit], YEAR(Orders[Order Date]) = SelectYear - 1)

- CY Quantity = 
VAR SelectYear = Parameter[Select Year Value]
RETURN CALCULATE([Total Quantity], YEAR(Orders[Order Date]) = SelectYear)

-PY Quantity = 
VAR SelectYear = Parameter[Select Year Value]
RETURN CALCULATE([Total Quantity], YEAR(Orders[Order Date]) = SelectYear - 1)
